  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Edward vs The Commissioner on 28 March, 2024 Author: G.R.Swaminathan Bench: G.R.Swaminathan W.P(MD)No.791 Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated : 28.03.2024 Coram The Honourable Mr.Justice G.R.Swaminathan W.P(MD).No.7918 of 2024 and W.M.P(MD).No.7193 of 2024 Edward, ... Petitioner Vs 1. The Commissioner, Tamil Nadu Food Safety and Drug Administration Department, Dms Campus, 5th Floor, No. 359, Anna Salai, Teynampet, Chennai-600 006. 2. The Designated Officer, Tamil Nadu Food Safety and Drug Administration Department, Food Safety Wing, Trichy District. ... Respondents Prayer : Writ Petition filed under Article 226 of the Constitution of In praying this Court to issue a Writ of Mandamus, directing the respondent to remove the seal put on the petitioner shop situated at Ann 1/5 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis Edward vs The Commissioner on 28 March, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/134836738/ 1 W.P(MD)N Store No.1, Jeevanantham Street, Thuvakudi Malai North Ayyampatti Road, Trichy District forthwith in pursuant to compliance of circular dated 04.01.2024 forthwith. Tt would have been appropriate, if he had been vending only grocery items. , the shop should be kept sealed for a period of thirty days. I had earlier held that such sealing cannot be done.",
    "facts": "Unfortunately, the petitioner also started vending banned Tobacco products. The second respondent rightly acted in the matter. The petitioner had paid the compounding fee of Rs.25,000/-. 3.As per the recent circular issued by the Government",
    "arguments": ""
  },
